Third-party software
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

octo-mail vendors its Go module dependencies under vendor/. Each vendored
module retains its own upstream license file (LICENSE / NOTICE) in its
directory under vendor/; those license terms govern the corresponding code and
are distributed with this repository.

Notably, octo-mail reuses the pure-protocol libraries of mox
(github.com/mjl-/mox) as an unmodified library dependency. mox is dual-licensed
under the MIT License and the Mozilla Public License 2.0; octo-mail uses it
under the terms of the MIT License. See:

  vendor/github.com/mjl-/mox/LICENSE.MIT
    Copyright 2021 Mechiel Lukkien <mechiel@ueber.net>

For a full inventory of vendored modules and their licenses, see the license
files under vendor/ (e.g. `find vendor -iname 'LICENSE*' -o -iname 'NOTICE*'`)
or run `go mod download -x` / inspect go.mod.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled shared junk model
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The default aggregate junk model includes features generated from project-owned
synthetic messages and these redistributable sources:

- LLM-Generated Phishing Email Dataset, Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/Dizzzy0x00/LLMGen-Phishing-Email-Dataset
- ActiveCampaign/Postmark Transactional Email Templates, MIT License
  https://github.com/ActiveCampaign/postmark-templates
- MailPace templates, MIT License
  https://github.com/mailpace/templates
- Mailgun Transactional Email Templates, MIT License
  https://github.com/mailgun/transactional-email-templates
- Keycloak Simplified Chinese email messages, Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak

The bundled artifact contains aggregate deterministic feature identifiers and
class counters. It does not include the source messages.
